  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find a past ticket that reports this exact problem, where Power Display switches to a different profile after the laptop wakes from sleep. The nearest tickets describe different problems. PowerToys#48774 is about a profile linked to Light Switch not being applied on wake. PowerToys#47951 is a title-only report that Power Display stops working after sleep, with no details. PowerToys#48428 is about a monitor not turning back on from standby. None of them include a fix or workaround. Please keep this ticket open as a new report. It would help to add a PowerToys bug report ZIP (right-click the tray icon, then Report Bug), the monitor models, and whether the profile change only happens with the docking station attached. Please also say whether profiles are linked to Light Switch or Night Light, since the theme change on wake may be what triggers the switch.\"}",
